Restore llama_backend_log_profile, which ollama's Go layer calls.

llama/llama.go calls C.llama_backend_log_profile(), but neither the declaration in
include/llama.h nor the definition in src/llama.cpp existed in any patch - they were
hand edits in the checked-in llama/llama.cpp only. A sync therefore deleted both and
the build failed with:

    llama/llama.go:761:5: could not determine what C.llama_backend_log_profile refers to

which is how this was found: reverting the tree and running the documented
checkout -> apply-patches -> rsync flow reproduced it immediately.

The body is guarded on GGML_USE_TSAVORITE while the symbol itself is not. Both halves
matter: llama/llama.go calls the function in every build, so it has to exist; but
ggml_backend_init_by_name("TSAVORITE") returns null where that backend was not compiled
in, and ggml_backend_log_profile_info then trips GGML_ASSERT(reg) inside ggml-backend.cpp.
That is not theoretical - an unguarded first draft of this patch built fine and then died
with "GGML_ASSERT(reg) failed" on the first request of a macOS build. An empty body is the
right behaviour there: no tsavorite backend, nothing to profile.

llama_backend_free gains the matching guarded teardown for the same reason: it was also a
hand edit in the checked-in tree and nothing else releases that backend.

diff --git a/include/llama.h b/include/llama.h
index a0a660bff..9ae511b57 100644
--- a/include/llama.h
+++ b/include/llama.h
@@ -399,6 +399,9 @@ extern "C" {
     // Call once at the end of the program - currently only used for MPI
     LLAMA_API void llama_backend_free(void);
 
+    // Call once at the end of the program to log profile - currently only used for MPI
+    LLAMA_API void llama_backend_log_profile(void);
+
     //optional:
     LLAMA_API void llama_numa_init(enum ggml_numa_strategy numa);
 
diff --git a/src/llama.cpp b/src/llama.cpp
index 74c49e651..25d0fcb8a 100644
--- a/src/llama.cpp
+++ b/src/llama.cpp
@@ -90,7 +90,21 @@ void llama_numa_init(enum ggml_numa_strategy numa) {
     }
 }
 
+// Guarded on GGML_USE_TSAVORITE, not unconditional. llama/llama.go calls this, so the symbol
+// must exist in every build; but ggml_backend_init_by_name("TSAVORITE") returns null when that
+// backend was not compiled in, and ggml_backend_log_profile_info then trips GGML_ASSERT(reg)
+// inside ggml-backend.cpp. An empty body is the correct behaviour there: nothing to profile.
+extern "C"
+void llama_backend_log_profile(void) {
+#ifdef GGML_USE_TSAVORITE
+    ggml_backend_log_profile_info(ggml_backend_init_by_name("TSAVORITE", NULL));
+#endif
+}
+
 void llama_backend_free(void) {
+#ifdef GGML_USE_TSAVORITE
+    ggml_backend_free(ggml_backend_init_by_name("TSAVORITE", NULL));
+#endif
     ggml_quantize_free();
 }
 
